{"id":"qzpyq-chemistry-biomolecules-biomolecules-test-1","_quizrrTestId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa","title":"Biomolecules - Test 1","questions":[{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a09de","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a09de","q":"Match List I with List II\n\\(\\begin{array}{|l|l|c|l|}\n\\hline & \\text{List - I} & & \\text{List - II} \\\\\n\\hline \\text { A. } & \\alpha \\text { - Glucose and } \\alpha \\text { - Galactose } & \\text { I. } & \\text { Functional isomers } \\\\\n\\hline \\text { B. } & \\alpha \\text { - Glucose and } \\beta \\text { - Glucose } & \\text { II. } & \\text { Homologous } \\\\\n\\hline \\text { C. } & \\alpha \\text { - Glucose and } \\alpha \\text { - Fructose } & \\text { III. } & \\text { Anomers } \\\\\n\\hline \\text { D. } & \\alpha \\text { - Glucose and } \\alpha \\text { - Ribose } & \\text { IV. } & \\text { Epimers } \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\\)\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:","options":["A-IV, B-III, C-I, D-II","A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II","A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I","A-III, B-IV, C-II, D-I"],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quizrr PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a09e3","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a09e3","q":"Glycosidic linkage between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></math>-glucose and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi></math>-fructose is found in","options":["Maltose","<p>Sucrose</p><p>&nbsp;</p>","Lactose","amylose"],"answer":1,"answers":[1],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quizrr PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<blockquote><p>Sucrose</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-8ea23a06db8aa15c.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 274px; height: 130px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-8ea23a06db8aa15c.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-8ea23a06db8aa15c.png\"></p><p>Sucrose is composed of a molecule of glucose joined to a molecule of fructose by an <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>-gIycosidic linkage.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Mannose is a sugar monomer of the aldohexose series of carbohydrates. It is a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math> epimer of glucose.</p><p>Fructose, or fruit sugar, is a ketonic simple sugar found in many plants, where it is often bonded to glucose to form the disaccharide sucrose.</p><p>Lactose is composed of a molecule of galactose joined to a molecule of glucose by a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>-gIycosidic linkage. It is a reducing sugar that is found in milk.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a09e8","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a09e8","q":"<p>The correct sequence of amino acids present in the tripeptide given below is:<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-88ac9371d2649718.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 393px; height: 190px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-88ac9371d2649718.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-88ac9371d2649718.png\"></p>","options":["Val - Ser - Thr","Leu - Ser - Thr","Thr - Ser - Val","Thr - Ser - Leu"],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quizrr PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p>Amino acids are organic compounds that contain amino and carboxyl functional groups, along with a side chain specific to each amino acid. The key elements of an amino acid are carbon, hydrogen, oxygen, and nitrogen, although other elements are found in the side chains of certain amino acids.</p><p>Peptides are short chains of amino acids linked by peptide bonds</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-237fa73fc7e7d637.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 253px; height: 481px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-237fa73fc7e7d637.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-237fa73fc7e7d637.png\"> </p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a09ed","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a09ed","q":"The correct structure of Ruhemann&#39;s Purple, the compound formed in the reaction of Ninhydrin with proteins is:","options":["<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool..app/pyq/jee_main/4c87288e-5c7b-47e5-8f99-8be5500f3503-0a0427b2-a31c-4e1c-9a32-d9d1d0bf62ac-image.png\" style=\"width: 317px; height: 144px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-e60fc6a86ed4be9d.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-e60fc6a86ed4be9d.png\">","<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool..app/pyq/jee_main/4f70e895-92e2-4812-8003-016863ccc145-image.png\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 126px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-0ac6c3d0ab62911b.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-0ac6c3d0ab62911b.png\">","<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool..a