ze: 11pt;\">&rarr;</span>iv, R<span style=\"font-family: Calibri, &quot;sans-serif&quot;; font-size: 11pt;\">&rarr;</span>ii, S<span style=\"font-family: Calibri, &quot;sans-serif&quot;; font-size: 11pt;\">&rarr;</span>i","P<span style=\"font-family: Calibri, &quot;sans-serif&quot;; font-size: 11pt;\">&rarr;</span>iii, Q<span style=\"font-family: Calibri, &quot;sans-serif&quot;; font-size: 11pt;\">&rarr;</span>iv, R<span style=\"font-family: Calibri, &quot;sans-serif&quot;; font-size: 11pt;\">&rarr;</span>i, S<span style=\"font-family: Calibri, &quot;sans-serif&quot;; font-size: 11pt;\">&rarr;</span>ii"],"answer":3,"answers":[3],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quizrr PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p>Structure</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool..app/pyq/jee_main/f081cf3a-4011-4b24-8ce7-d0d9372c16ce-9894443_5.PNG\" style=\"width: 209px; height: 221px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-26d735ae37c9af03.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-26d735ae37c9af03.png\"></p><p>Represents&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>&#8208;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>&#8208;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;Glucopyranose</p><p>Structure</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool..app/pyq/jee_main/e5cd207f-845e-464d-880e-511bb8aca336-9894443_6.PNG\" style=\"width: 201px; height: 211px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-a0c0b21d7d2f85fc.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-a0c0b21d7d2f85fc.png\"></p><p>Represents <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mo>&#8208;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>&#8208;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>)</mo></math> Glucopyranose</p><p>Structure</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool..app/pyq/jee_main/6b68da2e-86cc-4b00-8d1c-e95d6f968f72-9894443_7.PNG\" style=\"width: 259px; height: 198px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-8daa3baa03b19ac5.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-8daa3baa03b19ac5.png\"></p><p>Represents&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>&#8208;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>&#8208;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;Fructofuranose</p><p>Structure</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool..app/pyq/jee_main/e809c7e7-0669-466c-b690-029f2faa02ee-9894443_8.PNG\" style=\"width: 264px; height: 197px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-e0b0c58e14fd8d01.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-e0b0c58e14fd8d01.png\"></p><p>Represents <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mo>&#8208;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>&#8208;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>)</mo></math> Fructofuranose</p><p>So, the correct option is D</p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a29","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a29","q":"A polysaccharide &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math>&#39;&nbsp;on boiling with dil <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>393</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> under <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math> pressure yields &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math>&#39; &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math>&#39; on treatment with bromine water gives gluconic acid. &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math>&#39; contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi></math>-glycosidic linkages only. Compound &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math>&#39;&nbsp;is :","options":["starch","cellulose","amylose","amylopectin"],"answer":1,"answers":[1],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quizrr PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p>Cellulose,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msub></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool..app/pyq/jee_main/328484c3-7a57-49cd-810b-e7f5ee274014-image.png\" style=\"width: 322px; height: 200px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-5a613c162f375c58.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-5a613c162f375c58.png\"></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool..app/pyq/jee_main/b97a0eef-003a-4871-af8c-2d8eb85e6c0c-image.png\" style=\"width: 189px; height: 250px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-586f0d7c6ef70ee7.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-586f0d7c6ef70ee7.png\"></p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a2e","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a2e","q":"Type of amino acids obtained by hydrolysis of proteins is :","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>β</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>δ</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>γ</mi></math>"],"answer":1,"answers":[1],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quizrr PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p>Proteins are natural polymers composed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math>-amino acids which are connected by peptide linkages.</p><p>The smallest unit to which the protein can be broken down is called amino acids. The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math>-amino acids are the amino acids whose one carbon contains both the amino group <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced></math> and the carboxyl group <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>COOH</mi></mfenced></math>. This type of carbon is called <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math>-carbon. Thus, the amino acid that contains an <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math>-carbon is called an <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math>-amino acid.</p><p>Proteins upon acidic hydrolysis produce <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math>-amino acids.</p><p>Hence, the answer is option B.</p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa","_resolvedFrom":"official_bank_unique","_marksId":"6682bd2dba0e94a3c4025b02"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a33","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a33","q":"<p>Match List I and List II</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>  <td colspan=\"2\" rowspan=\"1\">  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">List I</p>  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Vitamin</p>  </td>  <td colspan=\"2\" rowspan=\"1\">  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">List II</p>  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Deficiency disease</p>  </td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>  <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></td>  <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Vitamin A</td>  <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math></td>  <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Beri-Beri</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>  <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math></td>  <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Thiamine</td>  <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math></td>  <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Cheilosis</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>  <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math></td>  <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Ascorbic acid</td>  <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>III</mi></math></td>  <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Xerophthalmia</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>  <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math></td>  <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Riboflavin</td>  <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>IV</mi></math></td>  <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Scurvy</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below</p>","options":["<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>III</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>IV</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>II</mi></math></p>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>IV</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>III</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>II</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>IV</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>II</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>III</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>III</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>II</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>IV</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>"],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quizrr PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<blockquote><p>Vitamin A Deficiency: Xerophthalmia: With this condition, the eyes may become very dry and crusted, which may damage the cornea and retina.</p><p>Thiamine Deficiency: Beriberi is a disease in which the body does not have enough thiamine (vitamin B1).</p><p>Scurvy is a disease caused by a serious vitamin C(Ascorbic acid) deficiency</p><p>Riboflavin deficiency is often associated with cheilosis (chapping and fissuring of the lips). Riboflavin Deficiency. Riboflavin deficiency can be associated with various developmental abnormalities, including cleft lip.</p></blockquote>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a38","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a38","q":"Identify the number of structure/s from the following which can be correlated to D-glyceraldehyde.\n\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-e89d26f0c0064bac.png?alt=media&v=stem2\"/ data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-e89d26f0c0064bac.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-e89d26f0c0064bac.png\"><br/>","options":["four","one","two","three"],"answer":3,"answers":[3],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quizrr PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-03950f7b7f2b0e0d.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-03950f7b7f2b0e0d.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-03950f7b7f2b0e0d.png\"><br>\n\nIn $\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{D}^*-\\mathrm{OH}$ group in right hand side then D-configuration is assign","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a3d","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a3d","q":"The correct match between item <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> and item <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> is<br />&nbsp;<table border=\"1\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>  <td colspan=\"2\">Item <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> (Compound)</td>  <td colspan=\"2\">Item <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> (Reagent)</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>  <td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>.</mo></math></td>  <td>Lysine</td>  <td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>.</mo></math></td>  <td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo></math>naphthol</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>  <td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>.</mo></math></td>  <td>Furfural</td>  <td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>.</mo></math></td>  <td>Ninhydrin</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>  <td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>.</mo></math></td>  <td>Benzyl alcohol</td>  <td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>.</mo></math></td>  <td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>  <td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>.</mo></math></td>  <td>Styrene</td>  <td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo></math></td>  <td>Ceric ammonium nitrate</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table>","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>"],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quizrr PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p>Lysine<math><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>Ninhydrin (this is given out by all the amino acids and Lysine is an amino acid.)<br  /><br  />Furfural<math><mo>&#8594;</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo></math>naphthol.</p><p>Rapid furfural test is used to distinguish between glucose and fructose. In this test, the sugar solution is added to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo></math>naphthol and concentrated&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math>.<br  /><br  />Benzyl alcohol &rarr; ceric ammonium nitrate.<br  /><br  />Ceric ammonium nitrate test is used for testing of alcohols.<br  /><br  /><img height=\"83\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-55055c4c3672ec9b.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" width=\"128\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-55055c4c3672ec9b.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-55055c4c3672ec9b.png\"></p><p>Styrene undergoes oxidation when treated with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>.</p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a6c","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a6c","q":"In an oligopeptide named Alanylglycylphenyl alanyl isoleucine, the number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> hybridised carbons is&nbsp;_____.","options":["","","",""],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"numerical","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quizrr PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p>An oligopeptide is a short-chain peptide. The given&nbsp;oligopeptide is a tripeptide.</p><p>The given Oligopeptide has the following structure</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-f04f0e131247c3f9.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 530px; height: 120px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-f04f0e131247c3f9.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-f04f0e131247c3f9.png\"></p><p>In&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridisation carbon can have one pi bond. The carbons marked with * are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;carbons</p><p>It has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridised <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> atoms.</p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a71","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a71","q":"The number of oxygen present in a nucleotide formed from a base, that is present only in RNA is","options":["","","",""],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"numerical","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quizrr PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-c7c31058b8d373a7.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 248px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-c7c31058b8d373a7.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-c7c31058b8d373a7.png\"></p><p>Nucleotide with uracil&nbsp;base present in RNA.</p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a76","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a76","q":"From the vitamins <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math>, the number vitamins that can be stored in our body is ______.","options":["","","",""],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"numerical","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quizrr PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p>Fat-soluble vitamins are stored in the body's liver, fatty tissue, and muscles. The  fat-soluble vitamins are vitamins <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo> </mo></math>. These vitamins are absorbed more easily by the body in the presence of dietary fat. Water-soluble vitamins are not stored in the body. The only <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> vitamin which is folound in liver is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>12</mn></msub></math>.</p><p>Vitamins <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>12</mn></msub></math> are stored in liver and adipose tissue.</p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a7b","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a7b","q":"The number of chiral carbons present in sucrose is &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;.","options":["","","",""],"answer":"9","answers":["9"],"questionType":"numerical","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quizrr PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fjee_main%252F67e4e1e5-293b-4fef-bbd2-8f8810423e9f-image.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F67e4e1e5-293b-4fef-bbd2-8f8810423e9f-image.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F67e4e1e5-293b-4fef-bbd2-8f8810423e9f-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 390px; height: 108px;\" /></p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa","correctValue":"9","_resolvedFrom":"official_bank_unique","_marksId":"648b5a68417cc3fb48d66b9d"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a80","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a80","q":"A peptide synthesized by the reactions of one molecule each of Glycine, Leucine, Aspartic acid and Histidine will have _____ peptide linkages.","options":["","","",""],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"numerical","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quizrr PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"Two amino acids join together and form peptide bond. Glycine - Leucine - Aspartic acid - Histidine","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"}]}